exit=0        # zero sorry
# PROVEN by real reasoning (not native_decide): a config with periods (p,0),(0,q),
# p,q>=1, has P_x(m,n) <= p*q for EVERY window (periodicity bounds complexity).
#   windowAt_add_period / windowAt_nsmul / windowAt_zmul : window invariant under
#     shifting the anchor by a period and by any integer multiple of it;
#   reduce_h / reduce_v / reduce_pair : anchor reduces mod (p,q);
#   periodic_pair_PatternLE : the p*q reduced anchors cover all windows.
  #print axioms periodic_pair_PatternLE -> [propext, Quot.sound]   (kernel logic;
                                        #  NO native_decide, NO sorry)
# Also proved symbolically in NivatTheory.lean:
#   sd_aperiodic          : the single-defect config (1 at origin) is APERIODIC
#                           (no nonzero period) — axioms [propext]
#   sd_PatternLE          : P_sd(m,n) <= m*n + 1 for every window (symbolic; uses
#                           encode_inj, the cell-encoding injectivity lemma)
#   nivat_bound_sharp     : Nivat's bound is OPTIMAL — sd is aperiodic yet has
#                           P_sd(m,n) <= m*n+1, so the threshold m*n cannot be
#                           relaxed to m*n+1
#   PatternLE_mono_K       : P<=K and K<=K' imply P<=K'
#   PatternLE_restrict_row : P_x(m,n) <= P_x(m+1,n)   (complexity monotone in height)
#   PatternLE_restrict_col : P_x(m,n) <= P_x(m,n+1)   (monotone in width)
#   -> all [propext, Quot.sound] only; no native_decide, no sorry.

